# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that the any measured phase corresponds to $\\theta = k / r$ where "
"$k$ is sampled uniformly at random from $\\{0, 1, \\dots, r-1 \\}$. "
"Therefore, we can use the continued fractions algorithm to attempt to find "
"$k$ and the order $r$. Python has this functionality built in. We can use "
"the `fractions` module to turn a float into a `Fraction` object, for "
"example:\n"
msgstr ""
